        <headline>Storm Warning issued September 25 at 2:48AM EDT until September 27 at 6:00AM EDT by NWS Upton NY</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...For the Gale Warning, northeast winds 25 to 35 kt with
gusts up to 45 kt and seas 12 to 16 feet. For the Storm
Warning, northeast winds 30 to 50 kt with gusts up to 60 kt
and seas 20 to 25 feet expected.

* WHERE...Waters from Sandy Hook NJ to Montauk Point NY from 20
to 60 nm, and Moriches Inlet NY to Montauk Point NY out 20 NM.

* WHEN...For the Gale Warning, until 6 AM EDT early this
morning. For the Storm Warning, from 6 AM this morning to 6 AM
EDT Sunday.

* IMPACTS...Storm force winds and hazardous seas will capsize or
damage vessels and reduce visibility.
</description>
        <instruction>Mariners should remain in port, alter course, and/or secure the
vessel for severe conditions.</instruction>
